#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""alexus: spawn a Claude Code, Grok or Codex agent and track it end to end.

Alexus, by Ragnarok. State for each run lives under ~/.alexus/runner/agents/<id>/,
or under $ALEXUS_HOME/agents/<id>/ when that variable is set. Settings live in
$ALEXUS_HOME/config.json (default ~/.alexus/runner/config.json). Run setup before the first start.

Claude is plain `claude -p` in a folder. Grok is plain `grok -p` in that folder. Codex is plain
`codex exec --json` in that folder. This program starts the process detached, records every event,
and keeps a live state file any UI may read.

  alexus setup [--owner NAME] [--who claude|grok|codex] [--handoff p1,p2] [--yes]
  alexus plan new|revise|create|edit|list|show|start|precheck|selfcheck
  alexus start [--who claude|grok|codex] [--cwd DIR] [--provider P] [--model M] [--name N] [--plain] [--no-plan] [--checklist FILE] [--domain FILE] [--handoff p1,p2|--no-handoff] [--] "task"
  alexus resume ID [--who claude|grok|codex] [--provider P] [--model M] [--approve-human|--no-approve-human] ["answer / context"]
  alexus handoff ID [--who claude|grok|codex] [--provider P] [--model M] [--handoff p1,p2|--no-handoff] ["note"]
  alexus list                                            recent runs, newest first
  alexus show ID                                         one run's state (JSON)
  alexus verify ID [--head HASH]                         check the hash chain; exit 0 if intact
  alexus receipts ID [--html FILE]                       checklist vs receipts; optional HTML page
  alexus stop [--force] ID                               stop it; it stays stopped (SIGTERM, or SIGKILL with --force, including a provider the first stop left alive)
  alexus run ID                                          (internal) the worker
  alexus selfcheck                                       fake CLIs only; no model call
  --help and -h print this usage and exit. A task that begins with a dash must come after --. Stdin and a leading space count.

PLANNING is the default. `start` with a task, and without `--no-plan` or `--checklist`, starts nothing
and prints one line telling you to run `alexus plan new`. `plan new` asks the CLI from settings (or `--who`)
to say the task back: UNDERSTOOD / WILL / WONT, optional WALLS, and a checklist. Each check is run once before any
work. A check that already passes proves nothing. Codex is held by its own read-only sandbox. Any other CLI plans
in a throwaway copy of the folder, so it cannot change the real one. `plan start` freezes that checklist and starts
the worker with the settings worker and handoff (`--who` overrides the worker). `--no-plan` is the only skip: proved
mode, and the worker writes the checklist. `--checklist FILE` is an approved plan. `--domain FILE` does not start a
run by itself; it can be combined with `--checklist` or `--no-plan`.

PROVED MODE (every runner, the default; --plain turns it off). The proof loop on top of the harness: the agent's
own "done" is not believed. With `--no-plan` it writes a checklist where every line carries a shell command that proves it.
With an approved checklist, that file is already frozen and the worker does not write the exam:
  - [ ] <what must be true> :: verify: <command>  [:: expect: <regex>]      - [ ] <claim> :: verify: HUMAN
The checklist is frozen the first time it is written (later edits can add lines, never drop or change one). When the
agent says it's done, this program runs every command itself, read-only (macOS sandbox: no file writes outside temp
folders, no ssh/scp/rsync). A failed check goes back to the same agent with the output; a round that proves nothing
new, or 4 rounds, is a dead end. When every command passes, a fresh critic (read-only tools) tries to show the work
is wrong; its refutations go back too. Outcomes: proved, needs you (only HUMAN lines left), dead end.

Files, per run: ~/.alexus/runner/agents/<id>/  (or $ALEXUS_HOME/agents/<id>/)
  task.txt        what was asked          events.jsonl   every stream event, raw
  state.json      live tracker state      worker.log     the worker's own errors
  checklist.md    the agent's proofs      checklist.frozen  the copy taken when it was first written
  receipts.jsonl  hash-chained receipts   (written by this program, never by the agent)
"""
import sys
sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
